 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 506981,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In a theater, the first row has 24 seats. Each row after that has 2 more seats. How many total seats are there if there are 40 rows of seat in the theater?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>This is an arithmetic sequence where the first term is 24 and the constant difference is 2.</p>\n<p>You want to know the sum of the first 40 terms.</p>\n<p>You first need to know the 40th term to use the sum formula.</p>\n<p>You can find the 40th term by using the formula: <span data-math=\"{a_i} = {a_1} + d \\times \\left({i - 1} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{a_{40}} = 24 + 2 \\times \\left({40 - 1} \\right) = 24 + 2(39) = 24 + 78 = 102\"></span></p>\n<p>Find the sum of the first 40 rows: <span data-math=\"{s_n} = n\\left({\\frac{{{a_1} + {a_n}}}{2}} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{s_{40}} = 40\\left({\\frac{{24 + 102}}{2}} \\right) = 40\\left({\\frac{{126}}{2}} \\right) = 2,520\"></span></p>\n<p>The theater has 2,520 seats in the first 40 rows.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "There are 2,520 seats in the theater."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
